@@ -0,0 +1,62 @@
+# AutoVideo 7.0.92: a stalled Flow image request stops cleanly, and the fix works on existing journals
+
+## What was failing (shot_020, job 20261022-143856-7-small-daily-habits-tha-9729)
+
+Runs from 15:59 to 16:52 IST, on the 7.0.90 code:
+
+- Each run opened the saved project, downloaded both uploaded references again (their Flow URLs had rotated),
+  then waited six minutes silently for a generated image.
+- No generated image was in the project. The retry repeated the same steps, then ended with
+  "Recovery needs attention". Every Resume repeated this, so the job could never finish.
+- Safe Resume blocked all generation and only pointed at a read-only preflight, so nothing in the app could clear it.
+
+7.0.91 fixed the identity of references for new journals only. It did not change the stuck state of this journal,
+because the old journal had no recorded labels.
+
+## What 7.0.92 changes
+
+1. **References are recognised by their live label and never downloaded.** Any tile labelled
+   `AV_<hash>_<filename>` is an uploaded reference. This works for journals written before this release.
+   Unlabelled tiles are still checked by their bytes, as before.
+2. **A run that finds no generated tile stops after one wait.** The request is marked
+   `recovery_state: no_generated_output_in_project`, and the message explains what happened and the one next step.
+   No further browser retries are made in that run.
+3. **A supported archive command.** `python3 cli.py v3 archive-request <job> storyboard/<image> --confirm-new-credit-spend`
+   renames the unresolved journal (never deletes it) so the next Resume makes ONE new submission.
+   It refuses when:
+   - the shot already has a downloaded image;
+   - the journal phase is not `submission_uncertain` or `submitted`;
+   - a valid non-reference image is saved (recover it instead);
+   - the job is running (production lock held).
+   Without `--confirm-new-credit-spend` it only prints a dry run.
+4. **Blocked-Resume message names the exact command** for each unresolved journal.
+
+## Steps for shot_020
+
+Approve the credit spend first. Then, from the install folder:
+
+```
+python3 cli.py v3 archive-request 20261022-143856-7-small-daily-habits-tha-9729 storyboard/shot_020_open.jpg
+python3 cli.py v3 archive-request 20261022-143856-7-small-daily-habits-tha-9729 storyboard/shot_020_open.jpg --confirm-new-credit-spend
+python3 cli.py v3 resume 20261022-143856-7-small-daily-habits-tha-9729
+```
+
+The first command is a dry run. Only the third command, after the flagged archive, makes a new submission.
+Do not run Resume again unless you approve another credit spend.
+
+## Installing
+
+- From 7.0.91: `python3 ../AutoVideoAI-v7.0.92/tools/update_v791_to_v792.py .` (dry run), then add `--apply`.
+- From 7.0.90: first apply the 7.0.91 update from the 7.0.91 zip folder, then the 7.0.92 update.
+- Stop the dashboard before `--apply`. Restart it afterwards.
+
+## Other notes
+
+- Default TTS split size remains 2400 characters.
+- `tools/update_v790_to_v791.py` is superseded and removed from `tools/`.
+
+## Verification status
+
+- Fixture tests: `tests/test_v792_stalled_recovery.py` (7 tests) reproduces the field state. All 7 fail on 7.0.91 and pass on 7.0.92.
+  Also covered: `tests/test_v791_reference_labels.py` (updated for the no-download rule), and the 7.0.90 and journal guard tests.
+- Not verified against live Flow. The shot_020 outcome is unknown until the approved new submission runs.
